{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "0fdb7295-e011-8808-aebb-9b2cbeb8bf50",
  "created_at": "2026-01-13T14:34:10-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Hector Ortiz",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:31:25-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:31:28-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hey Kevin. Is this the department that handles water, or the department that handles me yelling about water?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:31:35-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You got both. What's going on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:31:38-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So it's Spring Street, I'm at 410. Ever since that coastal storm Friday and Saturday, the street in front of my house is a pond. Three days later, still a pond."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:31:49-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Still standing water, three days out. Okay."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:31:52-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah. It all collects down at the low end of the street, and it just sits there. Cars come through and throw wakes like they're in a speedboat. I watched one slosh right up on somebody's steps."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:32:05-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wow. How deep are we talking?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:32:08-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "About up to the hubcaps. On a regular sedan, anyway. I'm not walking through that, I'll tell you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:32:15-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. So, Spring Street, low end, water about hubcap deep, since the storm. Is it draining at all, or is it just the same level?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:32:24-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Barely goes down. Maybe an inch or two overnight and then it's back. And honestly this keeps happening, every time it rains hard it's the same thing and nobody comes out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:32:35-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, I hear you. I'm putting it in as a drain and flooding complaint so a crew can go look at it. Is there a number I can reach you at if they need to check anything?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:32:48-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, 401-555-0171."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:32:50-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-seven-one. Good."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:32:52-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it. Hey, do the crews work weekends? Because if nobody can get here till Monday I'd like to know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:32:59-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "After a storm they sometimes do, depends how backed up the list is. I'll flag that it's been sitting for three days, so it shouldn't be at the bottom."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:33:09-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:33:11-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "And just so I get the notes right, you said you called in about it earlier, or this is the first call?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:33:19-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, this is the first one from me. I just kept hoping it'd drain."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:33:25-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fair enough. Let me read the number back, was it ten fifteen or ten fifty on the house number? Sorry, I wrote something down in the margin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:33:35-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Uh, neither. It's 410 Spring. Four-ten. The ten fifteen, ten fifty thing, you're thinking of the phone, no, that's... hold on, you asked about the time?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:33:44-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, my mistake. I meant what time you noticed it worst, around ten fifteen or ten fifty this morning, when the cars were going through."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:33:53-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh. Ten fifteen. That's when the delivery truck went through and splashed everything."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:33:58-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ten fifteen, perfect. Okay, Mr. Ortiz, it's logged. Somebody should get out there soon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:34:04-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thanks, Kevin. Have a good one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T14:34:07-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Stay out of the pond."
    }
  ],
